  "root_node": "model.stg_lineitem",
  "cause": "code_change",
  "action": "patch",
  "evidence": "The failing not_null test on stg_lineitem_extended_price reported 29,778 nulls. raw.lineitem has 60,175 rows, with l_returnflag='N' for 30,397 rows. The stg_lineitem model defines extended_price as `case when l_returnflag = 'N' then l_extendedprice end`, which yields NULL for all rows where l_returnflag != 'N' (60,175 - 30,397 = 29,778 rows). This matches the failing row count, indicating the nulls are introduced by the model's logic, not by missing source data. Therefore the problem started at the stg_lineitem model due to incorrect SQL, and fixing it (e.g., setting `extended_price = l_extendedprice` for all rows) will resolve the test."
}
